<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-01T11:53:15+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 01 Sep 2026 11:53:15 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Nasa scientists grew corn in space and found that microgravity changed root and shoot growth]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133610065.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[NASA's recent experiments indicate that corn seeds struggle with directional growth in microgravity environments. Without Earth's gravitational cues, the roots and shoots exhibit erratic growth patterns. Similarly, other plants like Arabidopsis thaliana face similar challenges in space. To prepare for longer missions, NASA is actively designing systems to counterbalance the absence of gravity, underscoring the importance of understanding plant behavior for future food cultivation in space.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nasa-scientists-grew-corn-seeds-in-space-and-found-that-microgravity-changed-how-the-seedlings-roots-and-shoots-grew/articleshow/133610065.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nasa-scientists-grew-corn-seeds-in-space-and-found-that-microgravity-changed-how-the-seedlings-roots-and-shoots-grew/articleshow/133610065.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T06:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133610277,imgsize-2177187.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Laurene Powell Jobs left Wall Street, then built a multibillion-dollar empire]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133670351.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/laurene-powell-jobs-left-wall-street-and-moved-to-florence-for-eight-months-then-built-a-multibillion-dollar-empire-funding-education-climate-and-social-change/articleshow/133670351.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/laurene-powell-jobs-left-wall-street-and-moved-to-florence-for-eight-months-then-built-a-multibillion-dollar-empire-funding-education-climate-and-social-change/articleshow/133670351.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T11:49:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133670590,imgsize-1580805.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California and Arizona turned old tyres into reefs and found 20 times more fish]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133653796.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.