-monroe-connection/articleshow/133669725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T11:22:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133669799,imgsize-1151536.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man buys late wife’s dream mansion, only to uncover $150,000 in hidden damage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133648043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-missouri-man-bought-the-1914-mansion-his-late-wife-had-always-loved-to-save-it-from-redevelopment-restoration-later-revealed-150000-worth-of-hidden-damage/articleshow/133648043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-missouri-man-bought-the-1914-mansion-his-late-wife-had-always-loved-to-save-it-from-redevelopment-restoration-later-revealed-150000-worth-of-hidden-damage/articleshow/133648043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T11:21:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133648399,imgsize-141414.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists find vast hidden water reserves beneath Oregon’s volcanic Cascades]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133647794.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/scientists-used-geothermal-drill-hole-temperatures-in-oregons-cascades-and-found-at-least-81-cubic-kilometres-of-water-hidden-in-volcanic-rock-nearly-3-times-lake-meads-capacity/articleshow/133647794.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/scientists-used-geothermal-drill-hole-temperatures-in-oregons-cascades-and-found-at-least-81-cubic-kilometres-of-water-hidden-in-volcanic-rock-nearly-3-times-lake-meads-capacity/articleshow/133647794.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T11:21:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133647998,imgsize-139490.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘The flood is on its way’: How 400 Nepal students escaped in time]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133669736.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/the-flood-is-on-its-way-how-400-nepal-students-escaped-in-time/articleshow/133669736.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/the-flood-is-on-its-way-how-400-nepal-students-escaped-in-time/articleshow/133669736.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T11:20:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133669786,imgsize-216284.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sea creature near Israel can regrow its entire body in just 40 days]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133658382.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scientists discovered a sea creature with remarkable body rebuilding abilities.  The solitary ascidian Polycarpa mytiligera regenerates from cut pieces into new individuals.  Researchers observed fragments healing and developing missing structures over forty days.  Major organs like the heart and neural complex were rebuilt by the creature.  This finding offers insights into regeneration mechanisms in solitary species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-sea-creature-near-israel-that-regrows-a-complete-body-after-being-cut-into-pieces-within-just-30-40-days/articleshow/133658382.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-sea-creature-near-israel-that-regrows-a-complete-body-after-being-cut-into-pieces-within-just-30-40-days/articleshow/133658382.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T00:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133658556,imgsize-161801.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Snails use calcium and collagen VI to make five types of mucus materials]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133659620.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Grove snails produce five distinct mucus types for varied purposes. Calcium and protein levels significantly alter mucus mechanical properties and functions. One mucus type lubricates movement, while another aids firm surface attachment. Defensive secretions and a shell-sealing epiphragm are also produced. This research reveals nature's sophisticated material creation from simple ingredients.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-how-snails-turn-mucus-into-five-different-materials-using-calcium-collagen-vi-and-changing-protein-levels/articleshow/133659620.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-how-snails-turn-mucus-into-five-different-materials-using-calcium-collagen-vi-and-changing-protein-levels/articleshow/133659620.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T08:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133659981,imgsize-111294.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spiders' stomach contents can reveal which insects and animals are living around them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662112.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tested-spiders-as-living-dna-traps-their-stomach-contents-can-reveal-which-insects-and-other-animals-are-living-around-them/articleshow/133662112.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tested-spiders-as-living-dna-traps-their-stomach-contents-can-reveal-which-insects-and-other-animals-are-living-around-them/articleshow/133662112.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T08:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133662112,imgsize-85246.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At 14, a Kerala girl built a washing machine that needed no electricity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133668500.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/at-14-a-kerala-girl-turned-an-everyday-bicycle-into-a-low-cost-washing-machine-for-rs-2000-that-could-wash-clothes-without-electricity/articleshow/133668500.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/at-14-a-kerala-girl-turned-an-everyday-bicycle-into-a-low-cost-washing-machine-for-rs-2000-that-could-wash-clothes-without-electricity/articleshow/133668500.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T10:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133668629,imgsize-2043535.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma man found at 92 pounds after addiction graduates with 4.0 GPA]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133668632.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/oklahoma-man-found-beneath-a-flyover-at-92-pounds-after-20-years-of-addiction-goes-from-homelessness-to-graduating-with-a-4-0-gpa-and-two-degrees/articleshow/133668632.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/oklahoma-man-found-beneath-a-flyover-at-92-pounds-after-20-years-of-addiction-goes-from-homelessness-to-graduating-with-a-4-0-gpa-and-two-degrees/articleshow/133668632.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T10:42:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133668969,imgsize-1595291.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Brazil’s humpback whales make stunning comeback; population surges from just 2,000 to nearly 35,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133644223.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Brazil’s humpback whale population has recovered from about 2,000 to nearly 35,000 after commercial whaling pushed the species close to extinction. Protection measures and a global whaling ban helped the whales return to Brazil’s waters. Scientists are now studying their migration, family links and behaviour, while tracking threats from fishing nets, ships and warming seas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/once-hunted-to-near-extinction-brazils-humpback-whales-make-a-stunning-comeback-population-surges-from-just-2000-to-nearly-35000-in-two-decades/articleshow/133644223.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/once-hunted-to-near-extinction-brazils-humpback-whales-make-a-stunning-comeback-population-surges-from-just-2000-to-nearly-35000-in-two-decades/articleshow/133644223.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T10:25:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133644846,imgsize-125159.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A man bought 51,000 acres of degraded land in Florida; decades later, it is the largest private restoration project east of the Mississippi]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133645561.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Advocating for biodiversity, E.O. Wilson suggests that dedicating half of Earth to nature is crucial for preventing a sixth mass extinction. In conjunction, M.C. Davis has embarked on an ambitious project to restore the longleaf pine ecosystem in the Southeastern U.S., investing extensively in native species reintroduction and tree planting. His Nokuse Plantation represents a major step toward preserving essential habitats for countless species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-man-bought-51000-acres-of-degraded-land-in-florida-decades-later-it-became-the-largest-private-restoration-project-east-of-the-mississippi/articleshow/133645561.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-man-bought-51000-acres-of-degraded-land-in-florida-decades-later-it-became-the-largest-private-restoration-project-east-of-the-mississippi/articleshow/133645561.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T10:25:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133645600,imgsize-2412885.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lindsay Clancy Trial: Matt Walsh slams jury delay; warns of ‘dire’ implications]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133665115.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Matt Walsh has strongly criticized the delay in the Lindsay Clancy trial, saying the jury should have reached a verdict much faster. Clancy is accused of killing her three children in 2023. Her defense says postpartum psychosis affected her ability to understand her actions, while prosecutors argue she planned the killings. The jury will continue deliberations Tuesday.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/the-verdict-shouldnt-even-take-17-minutes-youtuber-matt-walsh-calls-lindsay-clancy-jury-delay-a-total-travesty-as-deliberations-continue/articleshow/133665115.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/the-verdict-shouldnt-even-take-17-minutes-youtuber-matt-walsh-calls-lindsay-clancy-jury-delay-a-total-travesty-as-deliberations-continue/articleshow/133665115.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T05:02:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133665117,imgsize-1717962.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chapel Hill Appearance Cancellation: Club drops Clavicular after opposition; Raleigh show went ahead]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133664967.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Controversial influencer Clavicular’s planned appearance at Still Life in Chapel Hill was canceled after community members organized protests and raised concerns about his online conduct and history. The decision came two days after his Raleigh appearance at The Village nightclub. Clavicular, whose real name is Braden Peters, 